# Contributing

This project follows a lightweight, spec-driven workflow.

## Core workflow

1. Start from an issue.
2. For non-trivial work, write a short spec in `docs/specs/`.
3. Keep changes small and reviewable.
4. Prefer implementation in a single domain at a time.
5. Update the relevant docs when the design or product direction changes.

## Branch naming

Use a pattern like:

- `feature/<short-name>`
- `fix/<short-name>`
- `docs/<short-name>`
- `chore/<short-name>`

## Commit style

Use clear, imperative commit messages such as:

- `Add initial farm overview spec`
- `Document architecture and roadmap`
- `Fix parcel deletion regression`

## Pull requests

- Reference the related issue when possible.
- Keep the PR focused.
- Include a short description of what changed and why.
- Update docs and tests when behavior changes.

## Local development

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py runserver
```

## Testing

The project already has some tests in the `Fields` app. More test coverage should be added incrementally, especially for the `ERP` domain and tenant boundaries.

